error[trioxide(wasm-ineligible)]: `apply` is forced into WASM but can't be compiled: creates a closure
  --> input.ts:4:18 `(x: number) => x * 2`
      `apply` creates a closure
  --> input.ts:5:10 `double(n)`
      `apply` calls `double`, which isn't a function declaration the backend can follow
  help: only numbers, booleans, typed arrays, `number[]`, plain-data objects, local control flow, arithmetic, `Math.*` and calls to other compilable functions can be compiled (docs/PLAN.md §5); remove the directive to keep it in JS
